# PHASE 2 — Make the MVA genuinely usable (DONE on m3, VERIFIED on m4 except INTERPRET_SCREEN)

Add only high-value functionality.

Build on what Phase 1 already established rather than inventing a second
mechanism: every new action is a command registered with the dispatcher in
`src/rvw/commands.py`, reachable through `bin/rvwctl` and bound in
`hammerspoon/rvw_hotkeys.lua`. Screen capture belongs in its own helper, the
way audio capture does, so that its permissions and failures stay isolated.

Agreed hotkey scheme:

  alt-cmd-R        capture and transcribe (TOGGLE_CAPTURE)          exists
  ctrl-alt-cmd-R   capture, transcribe and analyse continuously     exists
  alt-cmd-E        explain the last 60 seconds                      exists
  alt-cmd-C        clarify the last 30 to 60 seconds                new
  alt-cmd-S        screenshot, save only                            new
  ctrl-alt-cmd-S   screenshot, save and interpret                   new, lower priority

## Multiple hotkeys

Implement configurable global actions:

### Clarify

Clarify/reconstruct the last approximately 30–60 seconds.

Useful particularly when speech recognition or an accent made the words difficult to parse.

### Explain

Explain the last approximately 60–120 seconds, especially:

* technical terminology;
* schools of thought;
* architectural patterns;
* unfamiliar conceptual references;
* implicit assumptions.

### Screenshot — SAVE ONLY

This is high priority.

On hotkey:

* capture the current screen or configured display;
* save the image locally;
* timestamp it;
* do NOT invoke OCR, LLM, VLM, or other interpretation;
* make no network request;
* avoid visible UI if possible.

The purpose is archival memory of what was on screen during the discussion.

Restrict the capture to the frontmost application's window if ScreenCaptureKit
makes that straightforward; a whole-display capture is an acceptable first
implementation if it does not. Save the image with a timestamp that can later
be aligned with transcript timestamps, and record which application and window
it came from — that metadata is nearly free now and expensive to reconstruct.

### Screenshot — SAVE + INTERPRET

Lower priority.

Perform the identical archival screenshot operation, then optionally pass a copy plus recent transcript context to a local vision-language model.

This action should be private and should not intentionally display anything on the conferencing/shared screen. Ideally interpretation can be displayed separately or retrieved with another command.

Do not delay SAVE ONLY while implementing image interpretation.

