# PHASE 7 — Two-Mac companion mode

Only after single-machine operation is mature.

The goal is to run the same assistant while separating meeting presentation from AI processing.

Possible topology:

PRIMARY MAC

* conferencing software;
* ordinary audio/video output;
* lightweight hotkey remote.

SECONDARY MAC

* receives audio/video;
* ASR;
* larger LLM/VLM;
* transcript/archive;
* assistant UI;
* screenshots/interpretation.

Investigate both:

1. software-based display/audio routing;
2. hardware capture, such as HDMI capture, where useful.

Important architectural requirement:

The user-facing commands and archive format must remain identical whether inference is local or delegated to the companion Mac.

The primary-Mac hotkey agent should require no screen, camera, or microphone permissions merely to send commands such as:

* CLARIFY
* EXPLAIN
* CAPTURE
* INTERPRET

Use a simple authenticated local-network protocol.

Do not introduce distributed-systems complexity prematurely.

